# Confidential case-study gate (/api/unlock).
# Set ONE of these on the server. Without either, the endpoint returns 503
# and the cases stay unreachable — it never falls back to a default.
#
# The digest is only ever as strong as the passphrase behind it: this is a plain
# unsalted SHA-256, which is fast by design and therefore weak against an offline
# dictionary attack on a memorable phrase. Use a long random one — six words from
# a large list is roughly 98 bits — and the offline attack stops being the risk.
#
# This passphrase reads the cases and nothing else. The studio has its own,
# further down: reading a client's outcome and being able to commit to the site
# are different privileges, so they are different secrets behind different
# cookies, and neither cookie is accepted at the other door.

# Preferred: the SHA-256 hex digest, so the passphrase itself is never stored in
# an environment variable, a dashboard, or a deploy log.
# Generate: printf '%s' 'your passphrase' | shasum -a 256
LOCKED_CASES_PASS_HASH=

# Or the passphrase in plaintext. Set ONE of the two — if both are set the
# plaintext wins and the digest is ignored, which is a quiet way to think you
# have moved to a hash while still running on the old secret.
# LOCKED_CASES_PASSPHRASE=

# How long a successful unlock lasts, in hours (default 2).
# LOCKED_CASES_TTL_HOURS=2


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The studio gate (/studio, /api/studio-auth, /api/preview, /api/publish).
#
# Its own passphrase, separate from the cases one, because this grant can commit
# to the repository. Set ONE of these; without either, the desk cannot be opened
# at all and both write routes answer 503.

# Preferred: the SHA-256 hex digest. Same rule as above — set ONE, and plaintext
# wins if you set both.
# Generate: printf '%s' 'your passphrase' | shasum -a 256
PUBLISH_PASS_HASH=

# Or the passphrase in plaintext.
# PUBLISH_PASSPHRASE=

# How long an unlocked desk lasts, in hours (default 4).
# PUBLISH_TTL_HOURS=4


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishing from /studio (/api/publish).
#
# Publishing commits a markdown file into src/content/writing/, so the post
# becomes a normal collection entry and goes live with the deploy that follows
# the commit. Without a token, /studio still previews and still composes the
# file to copy out — it just cannot commit.

# A GitHub fine-grained personal access token with, on this repository only:
#   Contents: Read and write
# Nothing else. Never commit it: set it in the Railway service variables.
PUBLISH_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Which repository receives the commit (default: this site's own repo).
# PUBLISH_REPO=danial-amin/danial-amin.github.io

# Which branch. It must be the branch Railway watches, or a published post will
# sit in git without ever going live (default: portfolio-instrument).
# PUBLISH_BRANCH=portfolio-instrument
